{"kind":"request","text":"C4 slot/edit contract: two concrete optional-field questions before the operation code. Section8 fixes item fields in the slot address; other fields are editable. The existing shaper permits an omitted optional item field, rejects null, and preserves given fields only. The validator also permits a default on an optional field; effectiveFields applies it later for selection.\n1. May an optional item field stay absent in a Slot? Proposed representation: only supplied item refs appear in the address; absence differs from an explicit ref, even if a declared default selects the same item. Required item fields still need refs. Derived selection through an omitted/defaulted field takes its basis at the first naming edit; no guessed seen value enters a ref. Current external decoder requires every item field and needs a disposition before that changes.\n2. How does edit clear an optional non-slot field, including a local-fact selector? Omitted patch fields preserve current values; null is not a valid fact/item value. A transient explicit undefined could delete that own property before storage, with only affected subjects recaptured, but this would choose an unstated edit rule. Please state the rule, or hold clearing explicitly. No undefined would enter stored data.\nNo operation source or public API implements either choice. The unrelated two returned-primary decoder inconsistencies are being repaired without changing these rules. LS5 gate continues unchanged.","body":{"conditions":"Resolve optional item-field address/default semantics and clearing an optional editable field before C4 operation code; no production or kernel change requested.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}